From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 23:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: Relock a PLL after a rate change only while it
 runs

A PLL with CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE is ungated for its rate change and gated
again before the clock core sends POST_RATE_CHANGE. The relock notifier
then waits for a lock that a gated PLL never reports, and warns after
70 ms:

  WARNING: drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c:38 at ccu_helper_wait_for_lock
  ccu_pll_notifier_cb
  clk_change_rate
  dev_pm_opp_set_rate
  panfrost_devfreq_target

On the H616 this is the GPU PLL: thermal throttling caps the GPU's
frequency while the GPU is idle and its clock is off.

Skip the relock for a gated PLL; it locks again when next enabled.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu_common.c
@@ -85,7 +85,7 @@
 	struct ccu_pll_nb *pll = to_ccu_pll_nb(nb);
 	int ret = 0;
 
-	if (event != POST_RATE_CHANGE)
+	if (event != POST_RATE_CHANGE || !clk_hw_is_enabled(&pll->common->hw))
 		goto out;
 
 	ccu_gate_helper_disable(pll->common, pll->enable);
